# MR.ducaysane — server-side credentials (TEMPLATE)
# On your computer: copy this file to `.env` (same folder), then fill it in.
# NEVER commit or share the real `.env` — server.py blocks it from being served.

# 1) Admin account — set securely with the script (writes the PBKDF2 hash for you):
#    python tools/set_admin_password.py
ADMIN_EMAIL=your-email@example.com
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=   <- written by the script; do not paste a plain password here

# Optional: session lifetime in minutes (default 240)
ADMIN_SESSION_TTL_MINUTES=240

# Optional: extra browser origins that may submit login/register forms,
# comma-separated (e.g. your production URL). The Host the request arrived
# under + X-Forwarded-Host are always trusted; foreign Origins are rejected.
# TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://your-domain.example

# 2) Supabase database (user accounts + SITE LOGIN GATE) — REQUIRED NOW:
#    every visitor must sign in (email + password) before seeing any page,
#    and accounts live in Supabase. Without these the site stays locked
#    (/login shows "database not connected"). Set with:
#    python tools/set_supabase.py
# (Dashboard -> Settings -> API: Project URL + service_role key — NOT the anon key)
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
